      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline alloy exhibits limited amorphous retention under rapid cooling.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline alloy has complicated crystallization behavior during thermal analysis.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 1–2 at% B will improve amorphous retention during rapid quenching and thermal stability during reheating.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add 1–2 at% B during vacuum arc melting and then melt-spin the alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooling at 10^4–10^6 K/s can form an amorphous phase in this alloy system.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Subsequent DSC reheating should be performed at approximately 20 K/min.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B addition enhances atomic packing and modifies local atomic environments.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The B-induced structural changes suppress nucleation and growth of crystalline phases.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B refines atomic packing and reduces free volume in the alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced free volume increases the kinetic barrier for crystallization during reheating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B promotes a more uniform amorphous structure during rapid quenching.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The B-doped alloy will show fewer and less pronounced exothermic crystallization events than the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The undoped alloy shows multiple overlapping crystallization peaks during DSC.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The benefit of B should be greatest at cooling rates of 10^4–10^6 K/s.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At substantially lower cooling rates, the benefit of B may not be significant.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessively rapid reheating may prevent the beneficial effect of B from manifesting.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Phosphorus and high mixing entropy promote amorphous-phase formation during very rapid cooling of Cr16Mn16Fe16Co16Ni16P20.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure of the B-doped samples to reduce crystallization events and maintain a more uniform amorphous structure relative to identically processed controls would falsify the hypothesis.",
